WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.387
What a working team does.

2
00:00:01.667 --> 00:00:11.160
Keep one screen per LLM feature, with headline tiles, cost, reliability, and quality, each broken down by model, prompt version, and route.

3
00:00:11.440 --> 00:00:17.157
Chart percentiles and rates by failure type, and include refusals and truncations as failures.

4
00:00:17.437 --> 00:00:31.411
Run graders on a uniform random sample off the request path, size the sample with the arithmetic above, correct the judge’s rate with measured TPR and TNR, and relabel a small sample by hand on a schedule.

5
00:00:31.691 --> 00:00:36.256
Watch inputs, outputs, models, and judges for drift against a baseline.

6
00:00:36.536 --> 00:00:40.333
Treat feedback as discovery first and a biased measurement second.

7
00:00:40.613 --> 00:00:50.683
Page only for symptoms that are urgent and actionable (availability, latency, cost burn), with multiwindow rules; send quality and drift to tickets.

8
00:00:50.963 --> 00:00:58.877
Then review the alerts themselves every month: which ones fired, which were real, and which incidents were found by a customer instead.

9
00:00:59.157 --> 00:01:02.272
That last list is your alerting system’s recall, measured.
